walk=[('01','Load configuration before the agent starts','package.json','The npm command loads the local .env into the host process. query inherits the server-side API key. The browser sees only a ready flag and model name.','tsx --env-file-if-exists=.env src/server.ts','powershell'),('02','Validate the student prompt','src/agent.ts','Reject empty or oversized input before the SDK starts. This keeps the classroom experiment bounded.',extract(agent,'export function validatePrompt','// Project'),'typescript'),('03','Call query once with explicit options','src/agent.ts','The prompt is a string. tools: [] disables built-in tools; allowedTools: [] would only change approvals and is not the same setting. This lesson also ignores filesystem settings, configures no MCP servers or plugins, disables transcript persistence, and uses one turn with a small SDK budget. The SDK manages its model interaction; there is no manual Messages API tool loop.',extract(agent,'  const conversation = query','  try {'),'typescript'),('04','Consume the async iterator','src/agent.ts','The for-await loop reads messages from the one query call; it does not make a new query for every message. A missing result is incomplete observation. finally closes the SDK query object.',agent[agent.index('  try {'):].strip(),'typescript'),('05','Separate text from the final outcome','src/agent.ts','Initialization identifies the selected model and tools. Assistant text becomes the answer. Only a result with subtype success and is_error false establishes success. Preserve other subtypes rather than relabelling them as completed.',extract(agent,'export function projectMessage','export async function runAgent'),'typescript'),('06','Forward selected evidence to the page','src/server.ts','The server writes JSON lines while the SDK runs. The response close event and a 90-second timeout abort this sample’s local run; finally releases the busy flag. These controls are web-app plumbing around the simple SDK example.',extract(server,'      const controller','      return;'),'typescript'),('07','Render returned text safely','src/client.ts','The browser assigns assistant text to textContent and keeps final status separate. The stream decoder buffers partial JSON lines, so a network chunk is not assumed to be a complete message.',extract(client,'    const consume =','    for (;;)'),'typescript')]
minimal='''import { query } from "@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk";

for await (const message of query({
  prompt: "Explain an AI agent in one sentence.",
  options: { tools: [], maxTurns: 1 },
})) {
  if (message.type === "result") {
    if (message.subtype === "success" && !message.is_error) {
      console.log(message.result);
    } else {
      console.error("Query failed:", message.subtype);
    }
  }
}'''
body='<section class="step"><h2>The idea in one small example</h2><p>This standalone illustration assumes the API key is already loaded into the process environment. The full app below adds validation, message projection and local web controls.</p>'+snippet(minimal)+'</section>'
